# One target configuration, two firmware images (katapult + klipper).
#
# The target choices live in the Klipper tree and are asked once: katapult's
# Kconfig defines the same symbols (architecture, processor model, clock
# reference, communication interface, bootloader offset) with the same values,
# so a choice made here is what both builds get.  `scripts/firmware-config.py`
# projects the shared, user-selectable values onto katapult's own Kconfig and
# lets katapult derive the rest (MCU, clock, flash geometry, HAVE_* selects),
# exactly as an in-tree katapult build would.
#
# `source` is resolved against $srctree, which the build points at the Klipper
# checkout; the nested `source "src/..."` lines in that tree then resolve
# there too.  Bootloader-only options (only katapult has them) are declared in
# kconfig/katapult.kconfig.
#
# Requirements and derivations:
#   - katapult supports the architectures its Kconfig lists (STM32, LPC176x,
#     RP2040/RP235x) and the processor models its arch Kconfigs list; a target
#     only Klipper knows fails the derivation with a message.
#   - the bootloader offset is the shared answer to "where does the app
#     start": klipper links the application there, katapult is told to launch
#     there (LAUNCH_APP_ADDRESS) and its deployer writes itself there.
#   - the USB device id is per firmware and is not merged: katapult keeps its
#     own (0x6177) so flashing tools find the bootloader, klipper keeps its own
#     (0x614e).  The vendor id is shared.

source "src/Kconfig"

mainmenu "klipperx firmware: katapult bootloader + klipper application"

rsource "kconfig/katapult.kconfig"
